     Use ``lzdcmp -b''; you may also need another option flag for dealing
with trailers, but I don't remember the exact one.  Alternatively, use the
VMS-specific syntax ``LZDCMP /EXPORT=(UNIX,NOENDMARKER)''.  I'd try the
simpler one first.

     NetHack 3.0j patchlevel 10 is available in VMS BACKUP format, via
anonymous FTP from host "uars.acd.ucar.edu" in directory "[.SRC.NETHACK]",
or via DECnet copy on SPAN from "ACDURS::SYS$LCL:[SRC.NETHACK]".  (Those
are just two different paths to the same place; ACDURS is 9.367 or 9583.)
Get file NETHACK.README from there for specific details.  NETHACK-SRC.TLB
contains a saveset of the full sources, packaged in a text library
container file.  NETHACK-EXE.TLB contains pre-built binaries, object files
in case relinking is needed, and data and auxiliary utilities for creating
a playground.  Both those packages are roughly 3500 blocks (1.75 Mbytes);
unpacking needs much more space (4-5 times that amount).  You only need one
of the two, and building your own binaries from source is recommended.  If
you transfer with FTP, those .TLB files require binary mode.

